    "body": "To get things going today, I looked right at that greater than 8 constraint at the bottom corner. Since we only had dominoes like [4,4] and [0,5] to work with, I knew those high numbers had to live in cells (2,1) and (2,2). It turned out the [4,4] domino sat horizontally at (2,0) and (2,1), which left the number 5 from the [0,5] domino to fill cell (2,2). That gave me a sum of 9, which is exactly what we needed to beat the target of 8!\n\nFrom there, the rest of the 3x3 grid fell into place like magic. Because cell (2,0) was a 4, and the sum for the region at (1,0) and (2,0) had to be 6, I knew cell (1,0) had to be a 2. That 2 was part of the [2,2] domino, which meant cell (0,0) was also a 2. Looking at the top sum of 3, if (0,0) was 2, then (0,1) had to be 1.\n\nThe final piece was the [1,4] domino. Since (0,1) was already a 1, its partner cell (0,2) had to be 4. This worked out perfectly because the last region at (0,2) and (1,2) needed to sum to 4. Since (0,2) was 4, then (1,2) had to be 0, which is the other half of the [0,5] domino we used earlier. Everything fit together so neatly!"
